# SCADA — Node-RED + Modbus (cleaned teaching notes)

Goal: upload code to the Controlinuo Mega PLC (Arduino-based), enable Modbus RTU and access PLC variables from Node-RED over USB (serial). Use node-red-contrib-modbus (Modbus nodes) and node-red-dashboard (UI widgets) for visualization.

---

## High-level workflow
1. Ensure PLC firmware/Arduino code has Modbus RTU enabled (serial/USB interface).
2. Connect PLC to PC via USB (appears as a virtual COM port; drivers may be FTDI / CP210x / CH340).
3. In Node-RED install:
   - node-red-contrib-modbus (Modbus nodes)
   - node-red-dashboard (UI widgets)
4. Configure a Modbus "server" (client settings) in Node-RED to use the COM port in RTU mode.
5. Place Modbus Read/Write/Flex/Getter nodes to poll or write PLC data.
6. Visualize values with dashboard nodes.

