## Modbus RTU basics (important concepts)
- Transport: RTU (serial) vs TCP (Ethernet). For USB-serial use RTU.
- Unit ID (Slave ID): identifies the target device on the bus. Typical single-device setups use ID = 1.
- Addressing: many implementations use 0-based addresses for node-red-contrib-modbus; Modbus documentation often uses 1-based. If values look shifted, try address ±1.
- Function Codes (FC) and conventional register ranges:
  - FC1 — Read Coils (0xxxx range) — discrete outputs (bit)
  - FC2 — Read Discrete Inputs (1xxxx range) — digital inputs/contacts (bit)
  - FC3 — Read Holding Registers (4xxxx range) — general-purpose read/write memory (16-bit words)
  - FC4 — Read Input Registers (3xxxx range) — read-only analog/measurement inputs (16-bit words)
  - FC5 — Write Single Coil
  - FC6 — Write Single Register
  - FC15 — Write Multiple Coils
  - FC16 — Write Multiple Registers
- Data types & packing:
  - Coils / Discrete Inputs = single-bit values.
  - Registers = 16-bit words. Multi-word values (32-bit int/float) require reading consecutive registers and interpreting endianness (word/byte order).
  - Signed vs unsigned depends on interpretation in Node-RED or post-processing.
- Polling vs Eventing:
  - Polling: Node-RED regularly queries the PLC at a configured interval (poll rate).
  - Report by exception: device sends updates when values change (requires PLC support).

