## Node-RED Modbus nodes (node-red-contrib-modbus) — common nodes and use cases
- Modbus Read
  - Purpose: periodic read of one or more registers/coils.
  - Configure: Unit ID, FC (choose coil/register type), Address (start), Quantity, Polling interval, Server (serial port).
  - Example: read holding register at address 0, qty 1, FC3, unit 1, poll 1000 ms.
- Modbus Getter / Modbus Flex Getter
  - Purpose: triggered one-off reads; Flex allows per-message FC/address configuration.
  - Use case: on-demand reads from UI button or flow logic.
- Modbus Write / Modbus Flex Write
  - Purpose: write single/multiple registers or coils. Flex Write accepts payloads/instructions dynamically from the flow.
  - Use case: control outputs or update configuration registers.
- Modbus Response
  - Purpose: used in more complex flows to form replies for server-like behavior (less common for simple client polling).
- Modbus Server (client configuration node)
  - Configure serial: COM port, baud rate, data bits, parity, stop bits, timeout.
  - Serial mode must be RTU for Modbus RTU over USB-serial.
- Notes on naming: different contributed nodes might use slightly different names; look for "modbus read", "modbus write", "modbus flex getter/write", "modbus response". Functionality maps to the FCs above.

