## Serial/COM settings (typical)
- Serial mode: RTU
- Port: COMx (choose the COM that appears when PLC USB is connected)
- Baud: commonly 9600, 19200, 38400, 57600, 115200 — must match PLC
- Data bits: 8
- Parity: None / Even / Odd — must match PLC
- Stop bits: 1 (or 2 if configured)
- Timeout: set to a few hundred ms (e.g., 200–1000 ms)
- Unit ID: set per PLC (often 1)

---

## Example Modbus Read configuration (typical)
- Node: Modbus Read
- Server: configured serial server (RTU, COM3, 19200, 8N1)
- Unit ID: 1
- FC: 3 (Holding Registers) — if reading memory locations
- Address: 0 (start)
- Quantity: 1
- Poll rate: 1000 ms (1 s)
- Output: connect to debug/dashboard node to view payload

---

## PLC memory mapping (Controlinuo / Arduino-based)
- Coils: used for outputs (single-bit).
- Discrete Inputs: physical inputs/read-only contacts (single-bit).
- Holding Registers: general read/write memory locations (16-bit) — use for variables, setpoints, configuration values; writable via FC6/FC16.
- Input Registers: read-only registers typically for analog inputs, sensor measurements, or other read-only telemetry (16-bit); accessed with FC4.
- Always confirm the firmware/PLC map for exact addresses and types.

---

## Example flows & usage patterns
- Read sensor value (holding or input register) every 1 s → format/scale value → display on dashboard gauge.
- Read digital input (discrete input) -> show binary indicator on UI.
- UI button triggers Modbus Write (FC5/FC6) to toggle coil or write register.
- Use Modbus Flex nodes to build generic read/write flows that accept msg.payload specifying address, FC and data.
- In Node-RED the Modbus read node typically outputs msg.payload as an array of values (for registers) or boolean(s) (for coils); inspect the debug pane.

