## Troubleshooting tips
- If reads return errors or wrong values:
  - Verify COM port and driver (Windows Device Manager).
  - Check matching serial parameters (baud/parity/data/stop).
  - Confirm Unit ID matches PLC.
  - Address offset: try address -1 or +1 (0-based vs 1-based difference).
  - Use a Modbus test tool (mbpoll, QModMaster) to validate the PLC outside Node-RED.
  - Inspect raw msg.payload in Node-RED debug to ensure expected byte/word order.
- If using multi-word types (32-bit/float), verify endianness (some devices are big-endian, some little; may require swapping words/bytes).
- Increase timeout if PLC is slow to respond.
- Check RTU framing/timing: inter-frame delays matter on serial links.

