## Teaching / lab checklist
- Ensure code uploaded to PLC has a clear Modbus map and Unit ID.
- On PC: confirm COM port appears when PLC USB is connected.
- In Node-RED: install node-red-contrib-modbus and node-red-dashboard.
- Create serial "server" node (RTU) and test a single Modbus Read to a known address.
- Add UI widgets to display values and controls to write values.
- Demonstrate address 0 vs 1 behavior and FC selection with examples:
  - Read coil (FC1) at address 0 → expected boolean
  - Read input (discrete input, FC2) at address 0 → expected boolean
  - Read input register (FC4) at address 0 → expected 16-bit measurement
  - Read holding register (FC3) at address 0 → expected 16-bit number (writable via FC6)
  - Write single coil (FC5) to toggle output
  - Write single register (FC6) to set variable

