## HMI (Node-RED Dashboard) — cleaned notes and usage

- Dashboard structure
  - Tab = page in the HMI (use tabs to separate screens/tasks).
  - Group = logical grouping inside a tab (use groups for related I/O).
  - Place UI nodes (buttons, switches, gauges, text) into a Group; assign Group → Tab.

- Button node (UI) — equivalent to Inject
  - Purpose: send a payload when pressed (momentary or toggle).
  - Configure payload: numeric (e.g., 1/0) for registers or boolean for coils.
  - Use two buttons for Start/Stop (payload 1 and 0) or one toggle button.
  - Set label, size, icon, color and tooltip (hover help).
  - Connect the Button node to a Modbus Write / Modbus Flex Write (or to a Function node that builds the correct msg) to write to a coil (FC5) or register (FC6).
  - For safety, prefer a confirmation flow or an interlock in PLC logic rather than direct dangerous writes from HMI.

- Writing flow examples
  - Direct: Button → Modbus Write (configured with address/FC).
  - Flexible: Button → Function (set msg.payload and msg.address/msg.unit/msg.fc) → Modbus Flex Write.
  - For registers: payload should be a number (16-bit). For larger types, send multiple registers or pre-format bytes/words in a Function node.

- Showing values/states
  - Text / Template node: display numeric or string status values.
  - Gauge / Chart: visualize analog values (temperature, level).
  - Switch / Indicator: show coil or discrete input states (on/off).
  - Connect Modbus Read → UI node to update display. Modbus Read (qty=1) outputs msg.payload (array or boolean) — use a Function or Change node to map to ui nodes (e.g., msg.payload[0]).

- UI editing & preview
  - Top-right menu → Dashboard tab: lists Tabs and Groups.
  - Use "View Dashboard" or the small preview icon to open the live HMI in a browser.
  - Deploy after changes to push updates to the running dashboard.

- Best practices
  - Group controls logically by function or subsystem.
  - Use clear labels and tooltips for operator guidance.
  - Validate payload formats before writing to PLC (use Function node).
  - Provide read-back and confirmation (read after write) to confirm changes.
  - Limit write access for dangerous controls; implement PLC-side safety.
  - For development/test use two Inject nodes (1 and 0) to simulate start/stop before mapping to UI.

- Quick implementation checklist
  1. Add a Tab and Group in dashboard.
  2. Add Button node(s), set payload(s) (1 for Start, 0 for Stop).
  3. Connect Button → Modbus Write/Flex Write (or via Function to format msg).
  4. Add Modbus Read for the same address to show current state → connect to Text/Switch.
  5. Deploy and test using the dashboard View.

